WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.436 --> 00:00:03.393
Unit eighteen. Human Rights Advocacy!

2
00:00:04.535 --> 00:00:10.684
Hello, everyone! I'm Teacher Vibol. Welcome to Secondary English, Level six!

3
00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:13.937
Hi, Teacher Vibol! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:13.987 --> 00:00:17.994
Today we learn: Human Rights Advocacy. Let's go!

5
00:00:19.364 --> 00:00:23.614
Human rights. Say it with me. Human rights!

6
00:00:27.137 --> 00:00:31.270
Advocacy. Say it with me. Advocacy!

7
00:00:34.735 --> 00:00:38.535
Justice. Say it with me. Justice!

8
00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:45.678
Equality. Say it with me. Equality!

9
00:00:49.135 --> 00:00:52.868
Activist. Say it with me. Activist!

10
00:00:56.423 --> 00:01:01.189
Awareness campaign. Say it with me. Awareness campaign!

11
00:01:04.678 --> 00:01:08.711
Legislation. Say it with me. Legislation!

12
00:01:12.196 --> 00:01:15.663
Dignity. Say it with me. Dignity!

13
00:01:19.157 --> 00:01:29.331
Grammar time! Advanced relative clauses. Listen. Activists, who often risk a lot, fight for justice.

14
00:01:29.381 --> 00:01:35.925
Your turn. Say it with me. Activists, who often risk a lot, fight for justice.

15
00:01:41.217 --> 00:01:53.036
Human rights advocacy fights for justice, equality, and dignity for all people. An activist often leads an awareness campaign to push for fair legislation and protect basic freedoms.

16
00:01:53.086 --> 00:01:54.561
I like this story!

17
00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:01.050
Look! What's the word?

18
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.250
Justice!

19
00:02:03.349 --> 00:02:08.488
Look! What's the word?

20
00:02:08.538 --> 00:02:09.779
Legislation!

21
00:02:11.038 --> 00:02:20.480
Think and answer. What human rights issue would you like to advocate for?

22
00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:21.771
Great answer!

23
00:02:22.949 --> 00:02:25.304
This unit's value is Justice.

24
00:02:25.354 --> 00:02:27.762
I can show justice every day!

25
00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:33.947
Great work today! See you next time. Bye-bye!

26
00:02:33.997 --> 00:02:35.771
Bye-bye, friends!

